{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKv5tfdaA7pAgybbmqGLUy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\tThis file provides guidance to coding agents when working in this repository.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Project Overview\n8\t\n9\t**QuantAgent** is a multi-agent trading analysis system that uses vision-capable LLMs (Claude, GPT-4, Qwen) to analyze financial markets in high-frequency trading (HFT) contexts. It combines technical indicators, candlestick pattern recognition, and trend analysis through a LangGraph-orchestrated agent pipeline.\n10\t\n11\t**Reference Paper:** arXiv:2509.09995 - \"Price-Driven Multi-Agent LLMs for High-Frequency Trading\"\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## Repository Structure\n16\t\n17\tThis repository is organized around three main axes:\n18\t1. Core trading / backtesting engine (`quantagent/`)\n19\t2. Applications and interfaces (`apps/`)\n20\t3. Documentation, planning, and operational context (`docs/`, `.beads/`)\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t### quantagent/ — Core Engine & Domain Logic\n25\t\n26\tMain Python package containing all trading, backtesting, and agent logic.\n27\t\n28\t#### Agent & Graph Core\n29\t- `agent_state.py` — LangGraph shared state schema\n30\t- `agent_models.py` — Agent-related domain models\n31\t- `agent_utils.py` — Shared utilities for agents\n32\t- `graph_setup.py` — LangGraph StateGraph definition\n33\t- `trading_graph.py` — Main orchestrator (LLM providers, graph execution)\n34\t- `default_config.py` / `settings.py` — Configuration defaults\n35\t\n36\t#### Market Analysis Agents\n37\t- `indicator_agent.py` — Technical indicators (RSI, MACD, etc.)\n38\t- `pattern_agent.py` — Candlestick pattern detection (vision LLM)\n39\t- `trend_agent.py` — Trend & support/resistance analysis\n40\t- `decision_agent.py` — Final LONG / SHORT / HOLD decision\n41\t\n42\t#### Backtesting\n43\t- `backtesting/`\n44\t  - `backtest.py` — Backtest execution engine\n45\t\n46\t#### Strategy & Assembly\n47\t- `strategy/`\n48\t  - `assembler.py` — StrategyAssembler (factory/builder for trading components)\n49\t\n50\t#### Trading Execution\n51\t- `trading/`\n52\t  - `order_manager.py`\n53\t  - `paper_broker.py`\n54\t  - `position_sizer.py`\n55\t  - `risk_manager.py`\n56\t\n57\t#### Portfolio\n58\t- `portfolio/`\n59\t  - `manager.py` — Portfolio state and PnL tracking\n60\t\n61\t#### Data Layer\n62\t- `data/`\n63\t  - `provider.py` — Market data providers (yfinance, etc.)\n64\t\n65\t#### Persistence\n66\t- `database.py` — SQLAlchemy engine & session\n67\t- `models.py` — ORM models (Order, Trade, Signal, etc.)\n68\t\n69\t---\n70\t\n71\t### apps/ — User Interfaces\n72\t\n73\tEnd-user applications built on top of the core engine.\n74\t\n75\t#### Streamlit App\n76\t- `apps/streamlit/`\n77\t  - `app.py` — Main entry point\n78\t  - `views/` — UI pages (dashboard, backtesting, configuration, replay, etc.)\n79\t  - `services/` — DB and backend services\n80\t  - `utils/` — UI helpers\n81\t\n82\t#### Flask App (legacy / demo)\n83\t- `apps/flask/`\n84\t  - `web_interface.py` — Flask demo app\n85\t  - `templates/`, `static/`, `assets/` — UI assets\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t### docs/ — Project Documentation (Source of Truth)\n90\t\n91\tStructured documentation, divided by intent. Read \"Documentation as a Single System\" in this document down\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t### tests/ — Test Suite\n96\t\n97\t- Unit, integration, and regression tests\n98\t- Testing conventions and setup described in:\n99\t  - `tests/README.md`\n100\t  - `docs/03_technical/TESTING_PATTERNS.md`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b9b65c5-e77e-400b-90aa-d1fae3699661","uuid":"fce4c2c0-29bc-4a8a-828c-bb7b019a6035","timestamp":"2026-05-09T02:39:13.027Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/AGENTS.md","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to coding agents when working in this repository.\n\n---\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**QuantAgent** is a multi-agent trading analysis system that uses vision-capable LLMs (Claude, GPT-4, Qwen) to analyze financial markets in high-frequency trading (HFT) contexts. It combines technical indicators, candlestick pattern recognition, and trend analysis through a LangGraph-orchestrated agent pipeline.\n\n**Reference Paper:** arXiv:2509.09995 - \"Price-Driven Multi-Agent LLMs for High-Frequency Trading\"\n\n---\n\n## Repository Structure\n\nThis repository is organized around three main axes:\n1. Core trading / backtesting engine (`quantagent/`)\n2. Applications and interfaces (`apps/`)\n3. Documentation, planning, and operational context (`docs/`, `.beads/`)\n\n---\n\n### quantagent/ — Core Engine & Domain Logic\n\nMain Python package containing all trading, backtesting, and agent logic.\n\n#### Agent & Graph Core\n- `agent_state.py` — LangGraph shared state schema\n- `agent_models.py` — Agent-related domain models\n- `agent_utils.py` — Shared utilities for agents\n- `graph_setup.py` — LangGraph StateGraph definition\n- `trading_graph.py` — Main orchestrator (LLM providers, graph execution)\n- `default_config.py` / `settings.py` — Configuration defaults\n\n#### Market Analysis Agents\n- `indicator_agent.py` — Technical indicators (RSI, MACD, etc.)\n- `pattern_agent.py` — Candlestick pattern detection (vision LLM)\n- `trend_agent.py` — Trend & support/resistance analysis\n- `decision_agent.py` — Final LONG / SHORT / HOLD decision\n\n#### Backtesting\n- `backtesting/`\n  - `backtest.py` — Backtest execution engine\n\n#### Strategy & Assembly\n- `strategy/`\n  - `assembler.py` — StrategyAssembler (factory/builder for trading components)\n\n#### Trading Execution\n- `trading/`\n  - `order_manager.py`\n  - `paper_broker.py`\n  - `position_sizer.py`\n  - `risk_manager.py`\n\n#### Portfolio\n- `portfolio/`\n  - `manager.py` — Portfolio state and PnL tracking\n\n#### Data Layer\n- `data/`\n  - `provider.py` — Market data providers (yfinance, etc.)\n\n#### Persistence\n- `database.py` — SQLAlchemy engine & session\n- `models.py` — ORM models (Order, Trade, Signal, etc.)\n\n---\n\n### apps/ — User Interfaces\n\nEnd-user applications built on top of the core engine.\n\n#### Streamlit App\n- `apps/streamlit/`\n  - `app.py` — Main entry point\n  - `views/` — UI pages (dashboard, backtesting, configuration, replay, etc.)\n  - `services/` — DB and backend services\n  - `utils/` — UI helpers\n\n#### Flask App (legacy / demo)\n- `apps/flask/`\n  - `web_interface.py` — Flask demo app\n  - `templates/`, `static/`, `assets/` — UI assets\n\n---\n\n### docs/ — Project Documentation (Source of Truth)\n\nStructured documentation, divided by intent. Read \"Documentation as a Single System\" in this document down\n\n---\n\n### tests/ — Test Suite\n\n- Unit, integration, and regression tests\n- Testing conventions and setup described in:\n  - `tests/README.md`\n  - `docs/03_technical/TESTING_PATTERNS.md`","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":321}}}
