{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WV5jENYhSJTyUP1Goy5qfv","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t│ ├─ TESTING_PATTERNS.md\n201\t│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-DS-<short-slug>.md\n202\t│\n203\t├─ 04_decisions/\n204\t│ ├─ README.md\n205\t│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-DC-<short-slug>.md\n206\t│\n207\t├─ 05_acceptance_tests/\n208\t│ ├─ README.md\n209\t│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-AC-<short-slug>.md\n210\t│\n211\t├─ 06_implementation/\n212\t│ ├─ README.md\n213\t│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-IM-<short-slug>.md\n214\t```\n215\t\n216\t---\n217\t\n218\t- `docs/01_requirements/README.md`  \n219\t  Current functional requirements index + links to per-change requirement files.\n220\t- `docs/02_planning/README.md`  \n221\t  Current roadmaps and phases.\n222\t- `docs/03_design/README.md`  \n223\t  Current technical design index + links to per-change design deltas.\n224\t- `docs/04_decisions/README.md`  \n225\t  Decision log index + per-change ADR-like entries.\n226\t- `docs/05_acceptance_tests/README.md`  \n227\t  Acceptance criteria / oracles index + per-change entries (Given/When/Then).\n228\t- `docs/06_implementation/README.md`  \n229\t  Implementation notes index + per-change deltas.\n230\t\n231\t---\n232\t\n233\t### Folder Semantics\n234\t\n235\tEach documentation folder follows the same pattern:\n236\t\n237\t- `README.md`  \n238\t  The **entry point and current truth** for that topic.\n239\t  Agents must read this file first.\n240\t\n241\t- `QuantAgent-<issue-id>-<doc-type-key>-<short-slug>.md`  \n242\t  A **per-change artifact**, linked to a Beads issue.\n243\t  These files are **append-only** and describe deltas introduced by that issue.\n244\t\n245\tFolders represent **types of knowledge**, not workflow steps.\n246\t\n247\t---\n248\t\n249\t### Versioning & Precedence Rules\n250\t\n251\t- Per-change files must be prefixed with the related Beads issue ID.\n252\t- Agents must never retroactively rewrite historical per-issue files.\n253\t- In case of conflict:\n254\t  1. Folder `README.md`\n255\t  2. Most recent per-issue file (by Beads ID / timestamp)\n256\t  3. Older documentation\n257\t\n258\tIf ambiguity remains, the agent must stop and ask.\n259\t\n260\t---\n261\t\n262\t## Beads (bd) Usage\n263\t\n264\tBeads (`bd`) is the **memory + task DAG** for ongoing work.\n265\t\n266\t### Core rules\n267\t- Every non-trivial change should map to a **Beads issue**.\n268\t- Each issue may produce one or more documentation files under `docs/`,\n269\t  prefixed with the same issue ID.\n270\t- Agents should query Beads to understand status and dependencies,\n271\t  and consult `docs/` for context and decisions.\n272\t\n273\t### Typical commands\n274\t- `bd status` — current state\n275\t- `bd ready` — work that is unblocked and ready\n276\t- `bd doctor` — setup health checks\n277\t\n278\t> Note: This repo uses the **`bd`** CLI (not `beads`).\n279\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b9b65c5-e77e-400b-90aa-d1fae3699661","uuid":"822f7e07-04b1-48ef-b912-3d15c8bd720d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T02:39:22.884Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/AGENTS.md","content":"│ ├─ TESTING_PATTERNS.md\n│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-DS-<short-slug>.md\n│\n├─ 04_decisions/\n│ ├─ README.md\n│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-DC-<short-slug>.md\n│\n├─ 05_acceptance_tests/\n│ ├─ README.md\n│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-AC-<short-slug>.md\n│\n├─ 06_implementation/\n│ ├─ README.md\n│ └─ QuantAgent-a3f2dd-IM-<short-slug>.md\n```\n\n---\n\n- `docs/01_requirements/README.md`  \n  Current functional requirements index + links to per-change requirement files.\n- `docs/02_planning/README.md`  \n  Current roadmaps and phases.\n- `docs/03_design/README.md`  \n  Current technical design index + links to per-change design deltas.\n- `docs/04_decisions/README.md`  \n  Decision log index + per-change ADR-like entries.\n- `docs/05_acceptance_tests/README.md`  \n  Acceptance criteria / oracles index + per-change entries (Given/When/Then).\n- `docs/06_implementation/README.md`  \n  Implementation notes index + per-change deltas.\n\n---\n\n### Folder Semantics\n\nEach documentation folder follows the same pattern:\n\n- `README.md`  \n  The **entry point and current truth** for that topic.\n  Agents must read this file first.\n\n- `QuantAgent-<issue-id>-<doc-type-key>-<short-slug>.md`  \n  A **per-change artifact**, linked to a Beads issue.\n  These files are **append-only** and describe deltas introduced by that issue.\n\nFolders represent **types of knowledge**, not workflow steps.\n\n---\n\n### Versioning & Precedence Rules\n\n- Per-change files must be prefixed with the related Beads issue ID.\n- Agents must never retroactively rewrite historical per-issue files.\n- In case of conflict:\n  1. Folder `README.md`\n  2. Most recent per-issue file (by Beads ID / timestamp)\n  3. Older documentation\n\nIf ambiguity remains, the agent must stop and ask.\n\n---\n\n## Beads (bd) Usage\n\nBeads (`bd`) is the **memory + task DAG** for ongoing work.\n\n### Core rules\n- Every non-trivial change should map to a **Beads issue**.\n- Each issue may produce one or more documentation files under `docs/`,\n  prefixed with the same issue ID.\n- Agents should query Beads to understand status and dependencies,\n  and consult `docs/` for context and decisions.\n\n### Typical commands\n- `bd status` — current state\n- `bd ready` — work that is unblocked and ready\n- `bd doctor` — setup health checks\n\n> Note: This repo uses the **`bd`** CLI (not `beads`).\n","numLines":80,"startLine":200,"totalLines":321}}}
